# Only the web app is needed to build the images (allowlist). Used by both
# ./Dockerfile and docs/aws/infra-example/Dockerfile.lambda (repo-root context).
*
!food-nutrition-app/
# The CDK example stages this context as an asset and must keep the Lambda Dockerfile.
!docs/aws/infra-example/Dockerfile.lambda
# ...and the Lambda image's start script (reads SSM secrets, then starts Next).
!docs/aws/infra-example/lambda-secrets/package.json
!docs/aws/infra-example/lambda-secrets/package-lock.json
!docs/aws/infra-example/lambda-secrets/start.mjs

# ...minus local build output, deps, secrets and dev-only files
food-nutrition-app/node_modules
food-nutrition-app/.next
food-nutrition-app/out
food-nutrition-app/*.tsbuildinfo
food-nutrition-app/next-env.d.ts
food-nutrition-app/AGENTS.md
food-nutrition-app/.env*
!food-nutrition-app/.env.example
# Local account data (APP_DB_PATH default) must never reach an image
food-nutrition-app/.data
# Only nutrition.db ships; stale copies/backups don't
food-nutrition-app/*.db
!food-nutrition-app/nutrition.db
food-nutrition-app/*.db-journal
food-nutrition-app/*.db-wal
food-nutrition-app/*.db-shm
# Tests aren't part of the production image
food-nutrition-app/**/*.test.ts
food-nutrition-app/**/*.test.tsx
food-nutrition-app/**/__tests__
**/.DS_Store
